DESCRIPTION:<p>Join us for the official launch of the IT-SAT 2.0 module! Th
 is webinar will provide comprehensive training on the latest cybersecurity 
 practices and policies to enhance your knowledge and skills in protecting o
 ur digital assets. Whether you’re attending onsite in Kuala Lumpur or joini
 ng remotely via Google Meet\, this session will equip you with essential to
 ols and insights to strengthen our organization’s cybersecurity.<u><br></u>
 </p><p><strong><u>AGENDA:</u></strong><br></p><p><strong>1:00 PM - 1:15 PM<
 /strong><br><strong>Introduction to the IT SAT Webinar</strong><br>Overview
  and objectives of the IT-SAT 2.0 Webinar.</p><p><br><strong>1:15 PM - 1:30
  PM</strong><br><strong>An Introduction to Security Awareness</strong><br>B
 asics of security awareness and its importance.</p><p><br><strong>1:30 PM -
  1:42 PM</strong><br><strong>Understanding Leading Threats</strong><br>Over
 view of current leading cybersecurity threats.</p><p><br><strong>1:42 PM - 
 2:15 PM</strong><br><strong>Insights from Security Policy Excerpts</strong>
 <br>Key takeaways from our security policies and how they apply.</p><p><br>
 <strong>2:15 PM - 2:21 PM</strong><br><strong>PCI DSS: Compliance and Beyon
 d</strong><br>Overview of PCI DSS requirements and compliance strategies.</
 p><p><br><strong>2:21 PM - 2:32 PM</strong><br><strong>Best Practices for H
 andling Card Holder Data (CHD)</strong><br>Recommended practices for protec
 ting Card Holder Data.</p><p><br><strong>2:32 PM - 2:37 PM</strong><br><str
 ong>Safeguarding Data Privacy</strong><br>Techniques for ensuring data priv
 acy and protection.</p><p><br><strong>2:37 PM - 3:00 PM</strong><br><strong
 >Incident Reporting</strong><br>Procedures for effective incident reporting
 .</p><p><br><strong>3:00 PM - 4:00 PM</strong><br><strong>Q&amp\;A Session<
 /strong><br>Open forum for questions and discussion.</p><p><strong>Particip
 ation Guidelines:</strong></p><ul><li>Join from a distraction-free environm
 ent.</li><li>Actively participate throughout the session.</li></ul><br>Than
 k you!\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
